{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And every meal-offering of a priest shall be wholly burnt; it shall not be eaten.</b> That is, every meal-offering of a priest — of a freewill offering — shall be wholly burnt, entirely given to the One on high. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: 'a priest' and not a priestess, for there is a distinction among priests between males and females in many matters: the meal-offering of a priest is not eaten, but the meal-offering of a priestess is eaten; a priest is warned against impurity but a priestess is not, as our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: 'the sons of Aaron' and not the daughters of Aaron. And the reason for this is that women brought death to the world. Likewise in the offering of sacrifices: a priest and not a priestess; and likewise in the eating of most holy offerings, such as the sin-offering and the guilt-offering and the meal-offering and the bread of the Presence: a priest and not a priestess; and likewise a priest is forbidden to a divorced woman but a priestess is permitted to one divorced; and likewise in the priestly gifts: a priest and not a priestess — they are not distributed by statute except to males of the priesthood." "<b>And the Rabbi</b>, of blessed memory, wrote in the Guide for the Perplexed that the reason for <b>'and every meal-offering of a priest shall be wholly burnt; it shall not be eaten'</b> is that every priest who offers his own offering does so in person; if he were to offer a meal-offering and eat it himself, it would be as if he had offered nothing at all — for from the meal-offering of an individual only the frankincense and the handful are offered — and not only is the offering minimal, but he would eat it and it would be as though he had offered no offering at all. Therefore they burn it entirely."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:26.413201177Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}